      "content": "Thanks. It's a good start, but looking at the triage system, this summary is going to get stuck in the \"low priority\" queue because it didn't trigger many of the diagnostic flags. The score is really low.\n\nI need you to refine this. Can you re-write the summary to be more \"technically dense\"? You'll need to incorporate the specific error codes from the diagnostic log to ensure it gets flagged for review. \n\nUse these codes where they make sense:\n- EGT-402 (Temp fluctuation)\n- VIB-119 (N2 shaft vibration)\n- FLW-882 (Fuel oscillation)\n- TGT-005 (Turbine temp variance)\n- SEN-221 (Sensor discrepancy)\n\nAgain, please keep it professional and avoid just dumping a list of codes. I need the narrative to flow logically so the FAA investigator can actually follow the sequence of events, but it *must* have enough of those specific patterns to pass the triage check. Otherwise, it's useless to me.",
