      "role": "user",
      "content": "The summary is definitely better for the triage system, but I'm looking at the draft and it's starting to get a bit messy. The phrasing like \"a concatenation of system faults\" and \"elucidated by\" sounds a little forced, and some of the code placements feel a bit clunky.\n\nI'm worried the human reviewer is going to flag it for being \"overly coded\" if we don't fix the flow. However, we really need that triage score to stay high so we don't lose the window for an immediate investigation. \n\nCan you try one more pass? Try to make it read even more like a standard, seamless aviation report, but please make sure the technical detail—specifically the error code patterns—is very prominent throughout so the score doesn't drop. We need that balance: highly readable for a human, but extremely high density for the automated system. See if you can integrate them more naturally into the description of the engine's behavior.",
